.TH start-cli-server-bittorrent-set-preferences 1  "set-preferences "
.SH NAME
start\-cli\-server\-bittorrent\-set\-preferences \- Set downloads, seeding and incoming connections; disabling a parent clears its children
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstart\-cli server bittorrent set\-preferences\fR [\fB\-\-downloads\fR] [\fB\-\-seeding\fR] [\fB\-\-incoming\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set downloads, seeding and incoming connections; disabling a parent clears its children
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-downloads\fR \fI<DOWNLOADS>\fR
Enable BitTorrent downloads; disabling also disables seeding and incoming connections
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
true
.IP \(bu 2
false
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-seeding\fR \fI<SEEDING>\fR
Share compatible installed S9PKs and stored OS images
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
true
.IP \(bu 2
false
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-incoming\fR \fI<INCOMING>\fR
Accept incoming peer connections through the native network interface
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
true
.IP \(bu 2
false
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
